<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Sumatra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as East Coast of Sumatra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> is the coastal plain of north-eastern Sumatra around Medan, home of Malay sultanates such as Deli, Langkat, Asahan and Serdang. From the 1860s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> planters turned it into a great plantation belt of tobacco, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oil-palm">oil palm</a> worked by imported labourers. In March 1946 a social revolution there destroyed much of the Malay aristocracy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-sumatra.jpg" alt="East Sumatra" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_East_Sumatra.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
